# Copy this file to signing.local to sign local builds with a specific
# certificate. The copy is git-ignored and must not be committed.
#
# When this file is absent, package-app.sh picks your local "Developer ID
# Application" identity, then "Apple Development", and only falls back to
# ad-hoc when neither exists. A stable identity matters beyond Gatekeeper:
# macOS binds Keychain items to the code signature, so ad-hoc builds lose the
# GitHub PAT and Google session after every update. The release workflow passes
# its own identity, so this file never affects releases.
#
# List your signing identities with:
#
#   security find-identity -v -p codesigning
#
# Use the full name when it is unique, for example:
#
#   SIGN_IDENTITY="Apple Development: Your Name (ABCDE12345)"
#
# If two certificates share that name, codesign fails with "ambiguous" and you
# must use the 40-character SHA-1 fingerprint printed by find-identity, for
# example:
#
#   SIGN_IDENTITY="0123456789ABCDEF0123456789ABCDEF01234567"
